    {
      "name": "cemu-a-wua-names-the-base-titles-save-folder-as-its-own-unit",
      "rationale": "The question names a .wua (Cemu's ZArchive) whose top level holds three title folders, named as Cemu's packer names them, <title id:016x>_v<version> (wxTitleManagerList.cpp:493 at Cemu 2.6): the base title 0005000010101c00, its update 0005000e10101c00 and its DLC 0005000c10101c00. A launch runs the bootable one, the base title (TitleInfo.cpp:217-251), and Cemu keeps its save in usr/save/00050000/10101c00 — meta/ and user/<account>/, user/common/ (nn_acp.cpp:57-69, iosu_acp.cpp:720-748). The answer is that folder with needs empty, physical through the usr/save symlink, and its unit own-folder with archive_folder the low word 10101c00 — the shape Argosy's WiiUFolderHandler uploads, <low>/meta/..., <low>/user/....",
